1
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,985
[tn]: So, you said the dhamma is directly visible.

2
00:00:24,192 --> 00:00:25,939
[tn]: I can see it here and now.

3
00:00:26,659 --> 00:00:27,507
[tn]: What does that mean?

4
00:00:28,252 --> 00:00:30,140
[tn]: How is the dhamma directly visible?

5
00:00:30,918 --> 00:00:38,371
[nm]: Because the dhamma is founded upon a recognition of the fundamental characteristics of your presently enduring experience.

6
00:00:40,035 --> 00:00:42,297
[nm]: So, the dhamma is not a mystical secret,

7
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:45,571
[nm]: the dhamma is discernment of what's already there in front of you.

8
00:00:45,728 --> 00:00:47,190
[nm]: What's already there in front of you.

9
00:00:47,744 --> 00:00:52,236
[nm]: My perception, my feelings, my intentions, that's already in front of me.

10
00:00:53,036 --> 00:00:55,622
[nm]: So, discerning the nature of those, means seeing the dhamma.

11
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:58,918
[nm]: Hence, dhamma is always in the present, and dhamma is always directly visible.

12
00:01:00,624 --> 00:01:08,761
[nm]: It's not that the dhamma will come through, like, oh, I have to be discerning this, discerning this, and then I'll discern the dhamma on some later occasion, on account of discerning this now.

13
00:01:10,492 --> 00:01:15,552
[nm]: You might develop discernment on a later occasion, on account of your efforts, beforehand.

14
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:19,024
[nm]: But efforts beforehand, you can't say that that's seeing the dhamma.

15
00:01:19,731 --> 00:01:21,596
[nm]: Once you see the dhamma, you saw the dhamma.

16
00:01:22,374 --> 00:01:29,497
[nm]: So, unless you see the dhamma, you should not regard yourself as somebody who is seeing the dhamma and practicing the dhamma, while at the same time knowing, I haven't seen the dhamma.

17
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:31,468
[tn]: So, can you unsee?

18
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:32,912
[nm]: No, of course not.

19
00:01:33,308 --> 00:01:39,558
[nm]: Because, again, it's not you doing the seeing or unseeing, it's you discerning on account of what's there anyway.

20
00:01:40,617 --> 00:01:44,947
[nm]: What... on account of things that are there, that cannot not be there.

21
00:01:45,446 --> 00:01:56,270
[nm]: In other words, you can discern this, or you can want this, or you can choose this, but one thing you cannot do, is not perceive, and not have feelings, and not have intentions.

22
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:57,286
[nm]: That's inconceivable.

23
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:02,313
[nm]: You might want to deny the arisen feeling, the arisen perception, the arisen intention...

24
00:02:03,801 --> 00:02:13,971
[nm]: but your acceptance, denial, both acceptance and denial, neither acceptance nor denial, mystification of it, is all in response to feeling, perception, intention, that are there on their own.

25
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:17,881
[nm]: And that's what you recognize, if you start discerning the dhamma correctly.

26
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:24,204
[tn]: Those are also indications, those things are indications of body.

27
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:25,430
[nm]: Of course, yeah.

28
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,271
[nm]: That there is a body.

29
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:30,956
[nm]: Yeah, there are many different approaches, but they would all be revealing the same principle.

30
00:02:31,305 --> 00:02:34,128
[nm]: Presently enduring, presently arisen, presently enduring things.

31
00:02:34,921 --> 00:02:37,240
[nm]: Which means, you are secondary to it.

32
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:42,044
[nm]: Your sense of ownership, your sense of choice, it's all real, but as secondary.

33
00:02:42,531 --> 00:02:46,934
[nm]: That's why, if you start seeing your ownership as secondary, it ceases to be ownership.

34
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:52,515
[nm]: Like, oh, you own this, but I own it more than you do.

35
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:55,945
[nm]: Which means, you're not truly the sole ultimate owner.

36
00:02:56,640 --> 00:03:03,062
[nm]: Yeah, you own it more than everybody else, but fundamentally, you don't own it, because I own it all.

37
00:03:04,028 --> 00:03:04,716
[nm]: So, you realize:

38
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:06,592
[nm]: Okay, so I'm onl y a relative owner.

39
00:03:07,276 --> 00:03:10,340
[nm]: And as such, can you act out of that ultimate view that you are the owner?

40
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:20,691
[nm]: That's why the Buddha compared generally, like sensuality, or even taking up this body, as like borrowing gold, and borrowing jewelry, and that you enjoy, and then you forget that it's not yours.

41
00:03:20,758 --> 00:03:21,705
[tn]: You're indebted.

42
00:03:21,814 --> 00:03:22,262
[nm]: Yeah.

43
00:03:22,371 --> 00:03:32,073
[nm]: You start acting as if it's yours, and then bailiffs come and knock your door through, and just start taking it, everything, and then you feel distressed and suffering.

44
00:03:32,752 --> 00:03:34,035
[nm]: But that's your own fault.

45
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:37,872
[nm]: Because you forgot that it was only borrowed.

46
00:03:41,392 --> 00:03:43,184
[nm]: So... and that's... that's that borrowing, like

47
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:44,940
[nm]: perception is there whether you want it or not.

48
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,140
[nm]: Feeling is there whether you want it or not.

49
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,779
[nm]: Intentions are there whether you want it or not.

50
00:03:48,841 --> 00:03:54,352
[nm]: Ignoring that they are there on their own, means you automatically took them as yours.

51
00:03:55,526 --> 00:03:55,990
[nm]: That's it.

52
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:02,710
[tn]: But then, if you don't take them as yours anymore...

53
00:04:03,730 --> 00:04:05,958
[tn]: that's the result of practice.

54
00:04:06,990 --> 00:04:07,980
[tn]: Those things are still there.

55
00:04:08,377 --> 00:04:08,844
[nm]: Exactly.

56
00:04:08,979 --> 00:04:09,897
[nm]: They were never a problem.

57
00:04:10,028 --> 00:04:12,550
[nm]: It was you taking them as yours, while they were not being yours.

58
00:04:12,825 --> 00:04:14,784
[nm]: Hence the discrepancy of suffering and dukkha.

59
00:04:15,084 --> 00:04:18,870
[tn]: And this, is this where conceiving, there's no more conceiving?

60
00:04:19,075 --> 00:04:19,859
[nm]: Sure, sure.

61
00:04:20,192 --> 00:04:24,540
[nm]: Well, conceiving is on the level of perception paired with the wrong view, basically.

62
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,803
[nm]: Perception of puthujjana already conceives.

63
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:32,544
[nm]: So, when a puthujjana perceives his perception, when he feels his feelings, when he intends his intentions,

64
00:04:33,465 --> 00:04:38,361
[nm]: automatically, just by doing it, so to speak, he does it as it's his own.

65
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:46,134
[nm]: His view puts himself first, despite the the evidence showing the contrary, which is...

66
00:04:46,512 --> 00:04:51,766
[nm]: No. You have the view, you have the attitude, because these things are there on their own, enduring.

67
00:04:54,809 --> 00:05:00,851
[nm]: So, all a puthujana would need to do is stop fueling that attitude of taking it for granted as I am the first,

68
00:05:01,356 --> 00:05:05,078
[nm]: and start undoing in his own experience, like, what am I feeling right now?

69
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:10,889
[nm]: I'm feeling, I don't know, quite pleasantly, sort of, elated mood.

70
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,521
[nm]: Okay, that's very good.

71
00:05:13,049 --> 00:05:17,948
[nm]: Describe the characteristics and the signs of that mood to yourself, out loud, if you want.

72
00:05:19,219 --> 00:05:25,337
[nm]: Well, the first and obvious thing, whenever we've done this in practice with other people, the answer would be, it's just there.

73
00:05:26,643 --> 00:05:30,512
[nm]: Okay, so, what would be the signs and characteristics of something that's just there?

74
00:05:31,568 --> 00:05:33,689
[nm]: Means it's kind of independent of you, isn't it?

75
00:05:34,345 --> 00:05:35,216
[nm]: It's just there.

76
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:42,707
[nm]: I can move it left, I can move it right, I can do this, I can do that, but fundamentally, I could do any of those things because this thing is just there.

77
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:45,904
[nm]: So, if something is just there, you haven't created it.

78
00:05:46,156 --> 00:05:48,268
[nm]: It was just there, you found it as such.

79
00:05:49,484 --> 00:05:57,379
[nm]: But, by not thinking these things, puthujjana, just there, means for me, means my, because I already am.

80
00:05:57,952 --> 00:06:05,148
[nm]: Failing to see that I already am, and for me, and mine, is because this thing is just there, and it's still just there.

81
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:12,979
[nm]: Which means, when it ceases to be just there, you won't be able to stand a second longer, independently of it.

82
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:24,118
[nm]: So, it's really just about dwelling on these characteristics and knowing how to question yourself rightly, to start discerning the characteristics of things that are in the things.

83
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:30,438
[nm]: That's why the Buddha described anicca and dukkha as inherent in all these determinations of your sense of self.

84
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:33,971
[nm]: He didn't say that's impermanent, that's impermanent, that's impermanent.

85
00:06:34,089 --> 00:06:34,320
[nm]: No.

86
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:37,090
[nm]: He said things that determine you are impermanent.

87
00:06:37,090 --> 00:06:38,867
[nm]: Things that determine you are suffering.

88
00:06:39,206 --> 00:06:42,364
[nm]: Because of that, things that you are, are not yourself.

89
00:06:43,142 --> 00:06:44,022
[nm]: Things that you are,

90
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,846
[nm]: it's not you, so to speak.

91
00:06:45,974 --> 00:06:46,956
[nm]: It cannot be yours.

92
00:06:48,592 --> 00:06:49,878
[nm]: And that's the whole point here.

93
00:06:50,330 --> 00:06:54,387
[nm]: You recognize things that determine you are these things that are just there.

94
00:06:55,686 --> 00:07:09,630
[nm]: So, by dwelling on the themes of characteristics of things that are just there, you're actually dwelling on the theme and the characteristics of impermanence, of suffering, as in unsatisfactory, disease.

95
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:11,001
[nm]: Oh, it's just there. Mhmm...

96
00:07:11,385 --> 00:07:12,377
[nm]: Is it threatening?

97
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:14,108
[nm]: Who brought this?

98
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:14,550
[nm]: I don't know.

99
00:07:14,550 --> 00:07:16,185
[nm]: Nobody knows how this came to be.

100
00:07:16,537 --> 00:07:17,590
[nm]: Yet, it's just there.

101
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:21,926
[nm]: Yet, my whole experience is directed upon, determined by it.

102
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:23,596
[nm]: What if this goes?

103
00:07:23,705 --> 00:07:24,064
[tn]: Yeah.

104
00:07:24,281 --> 00:07:28,563
[tn]: That thing stands upon that which I've got no access to.

105
00:07:28,662 --> 00:07:32,841
[nm]: Even the thought that it stands upon that, already stands upon that.

106
00:07:34,250 --> 00:07:37,932
[tn]: But the basis of feeling that thing that's already there... Inconceivable.

107
00:07:39,609 --> 00:07:41,276
[nm]: Inconceivable. Inconceivable

108
00:07:41,312 --> 00:07:42,508
[tn]: It's inconceivable to me.

109
00:07:42,812 --> 00:07:43,356
[nm]: Exactly.

110
00:07:44,265 --> 00:07:47,785
[nm]: So, it's not like you're looking for a great revelation, epiphany.

111
00:07:48,028 --> 00:07:51,052
[nm]: You're just dwelling on those particular characteristics.

112
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:59,974
[nm]: And that, in itself, is going to result in basically diminishing of the symptoms of non-dwelling on those things.

113
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:10,534
[nm]: By not dwelling on things just being there, by not dwelling on that impermanence, you automatically assume permanence, you automatically assume ownership.

114
00:08:13,635 --> 00:08:24,163
[nm]: By dwelling on that, oh, this is just there, independent of me, kind of indifferent to me, I can react, I can do this, but fundamentally, I can do any of it, because this thing is enduring on its own.

115
00:08:25,395 --> 00:08:39,260
[nm]: Discerning that more and more, means discerning the theme of impermanence more and more, which then automatically means discerning the theme of this is more and more, dukkha, and results in the experience of not being taken as myself.

116
00:08:46,854 --> 00:08:51,920
[tn]: So, if one has... starts having views about, say, feelings, why they're there?

117
00:08:52,810 --> 00:08:54,566
[tn]: Feelings are there because...

118
00:08:55,174 --> 00:09:00,190
[nm]: See, you can even... you can even... the only reason you're even able to ask such question, why are feelings there?

119
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:01,968
[nm]: Because feeling is there during on its own.

120
00:09:03,369 --> 00:09:10,643
[nm]: It doesn't mean any thought, any response, any logical, rational turn is already secondary to this thing being there.

121
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:14,851
[nm]: That's why dhamma is beyond thinking, as in [?atakka], which cannot be reasoned.

122
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:16,416
[nm]: Doesn't mean it's mystical,

123
00:09:16,592 --> 00:09:21,558
[nm]: means that movements of your reason cannot stand for that because of which these movements are.

124
00:09:22,086 --> 00:09:25,008
[nm]: Cannot stand for the nature of things, which is what dhamma is.

125
00:09:25,388 --> 00:09:31,180
[nm]: But, as we've shown, you can still use these movements to learn how to look the opposite direction of the movement.

126
00:09:31,382 --> 00:09:33,430
[nm]: To look at the source of the movement.

127
00:09:34,057 --> 00:09:36,800
[nm]: Source being yoniso, like yoniso manasikāra.

128
00:09:38,825 --> 00:09:40,840
[nm]: So, you have a... oh, how are these feelings there?

129
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:41,654
[nm]: What is my feeling?

130
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:42,732
[nm]: So, that's a movement.

131
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:44,358
[nm]: That's a rational thought, question.

132
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:52,377
[nm]: But, instead of just trying to find another rational answer, you start looking for the direction where this question is pointing at.

133
00:09:52,579 --> 00:09:56,889
[nm]: Means, the fact that you can ask, well, what is my current feeling?

134
00:09:57,692 --> 00:09:58,710
[nm]: Means, the feeling is there.

135
00:09:59,996 --> 00:10:02,940
[nm]: Your designation, your directing of the question,

136
00:10:03,929 --> 00:10:06,630
[nm]: would not be possible if the feeling is not there enduring.

137
00:10:06,928 --> 00:10:13,516
[nm]: So, you might not know the particulars of the feeling, but the fact that, even in the most ambiguous terms, you go: how do I feel now?

138
00:10:13,545 --> 00:10:16,406
[nm]: There is some sense of the direction where the feeling is.

139
00:10:17,532 --> 00:10:20,908
[nm]: But instead of providing the answer, you start looking down that direction.

140
00:10:21,232 --> 00:10:21,769
[nm]: How am I feeling?

141
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,838
[nm]: Well, I'm not sure.

142
00:10:23,555 --> 00:10:30,393
[nm]: Okay, so that lack of... lack of kind of... being not sure, how does that feel then?

143
00:10:31,171 --> 00:10:33,491
[nm]: Well, it kind of feels a bit pressing.

144
00:10:33,817 --> 00:10:35,232
[nm]: What does pressure feel like?

145
00:10:35,472 --> 00:10:36,140
[nm]: It's unpleasant.

146
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:42,102
[nm]: Okay, so then, me not being sure how I feel slightly pressured by it, means I feel unpleasantly.

147
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,705
[nm]: Fundamentally, on a subtle level, it's unpleasant.

148
00:10:45,929 --> 00:10:51,676
[nm]: What are the characteristics of that unpleasant feeling that's presently enduring while I'm asking these questions?

149
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:57,050
[nm]: So, see, like, as I said, you use the movements of your question, but you don't follow the direction of the movement.

150
00:10:57,050 --> 00:10:58,208
[nm]: You look at the source of it.

151
00:10:58,601 --> 00:10:59,836
[nm]: You learn how to see

152
00:11:00,659 --> 00:11:07,382
[nm]: the background of that movement, the foundation, the source. Which is literally, womb of the... where the movement came from.

153
00:11:08,425 --> 00:11:11,868
[nm]: And that's what the Buddha meant by yoni... yoniso, yoni means womb, literally.

154
00:11:13,363 --> 00:11:18,009
[nm]: So, you learn how to attend the source, as opposed to attend what that sort of question points you at.

155
00:11:19,072 --> 00:11:23,459
[nm]: And that's how you get to discern more and more characteristics of that which is already there.

156
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,908
[nm]: That feeling is already there, whether you want it or not.

157
00:11:28,342 --> 00:11:30,601
[nm]: The mood is already there, whether you want it or not.

158
00:11:33,078 --> 00:11:42,054
[nm]: And I talk about the mood because the mood is kind of a blend between general perception and general feeling, how you feel it, which is basically the mood is where your mind is.

159
00:11:44,496 --> 00:11:46,441
[nm]: But you can't see directly, oh, this is my mood.

160
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:46,680
[nm]: No.

161
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,083
[nm]: It's always behind you.

162
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:55,548
[nm]: But if you never learn how to look in the direction from that source, you can never see it, which means you're always going to be affected by it.

163
00:11:55,897 --> 00:11:59,049
[nm]: That's when people go through their moods, like on a daily basis, up and down.

164
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:08,851
[tn]: And someone who doesn't see their mind, or the signs of the mind...

165
00:12:08,850 --> 00:12:10,998
[nm]: Means they're automatically affected by it.

166
00:12:11,228 --> 00:12:12,435
[tn]: And so in solitude...

167
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:29,017
[nm]: In solitude, it's going to become hard to not see the signs of your mind, which is why people who exist in the mode of avoiding the states of the... avoiding seeing the states of the mind, but just going with what direction is offered through their senses,

168
00:12:29,561 --> 00:12:36,969
[nm]: distraction, sensuality, ill-will, I'm angry, I'm sad, I'm happy, I'm lustful, I'm this, I'm this, I'm this... Never stop and look at the source of it.

169
00:12:37,488 --> 00:12:39,507
[nm]: That's why those people are terrified of solitude.

170
00:12:39,936 --> 00:12:41,603
[nm]: It feels like drowning, literally.

171
00:12:42,153 --> 00:12:47,875
[nm]: The more of existence you go used to, the threshold of being of that bhava, it's not being matched.

172
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:55,830
[nm]: There isn't that level of engagement, that level of... of sort of a degree of consciousness in those things, and you feel like you're drowning.

173
00:12:55,830 --> 00:12:58,384
[nm]: That's why people get panic attacks and anxieties and...

174
00:12:58,841 --> 00:13:00,370
[nm]: Dread and overwhelm, basically.

175
00:13:00,370 --> 00:13:01,148
[nm]: Just by solitude,

176
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:01,790
[nm]: go mad.

177
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:02,726
[tn]: Yeah, yeah.

178
00:13:03,430 --> 00:13:05,609
[nm]: But you don't go mad because of the solitude.

179
00:13:06,092 --> 00:13:12,227
[nm]: You go mad on account of not being able to fulfill the habits of avoiding solitude that you existentially depend upon.

180
00:13:13,283 --> 00:13:14,172
[nm]: That's why you go mad.

181
00:13:14,352 --> 00:13:18,451
[nm]: So, if you start undoing those habits, you start seeing solitude as pleasant.

182
00:13:19,027 --> 00:13:20,348
[nm]: You start seeing boredom.

183
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:22,304
[nm]: Well, boredom has negative connotation.

184
00:13:22,515 --> 00:13:24,288
[nm]: Neutral, neither pleasant or unpleasant.

185
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:26,588
[nm]: You start feeling as lofty and pleasant.

186
00:13:26,870 --> 00:13:27,849
[nm]: You start delighting in it.

187
00:13:31,024 --> 00:13:38,793
[nm]: Like, boredom is a neutral feeling from the point of view of unmatched, unmet habits of distraction.

188
00:13:39,443 --> 00:13:42,480
[nm]: I'm bored, because I still assume I must be doing something.

189
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,278
[nm]: I want to be doing something.

190
00:13:45,110 --> 00:13:46,384
[nm]: But it's nothing I have to...

191
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,776
[nm]: I can't do now, or nothing that I particularly want to do...

192
00:13:49,929 --> 00:13:51,251
[nm]: So, I'm kind of a bit bored.

193
00:13:51,379 --> 00:13:54,220
[nm]: You stay with that boredom, and then that discrepancy is going to get amplified.

194
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:59,952
[nm]: Like, your dependence on needing to do something, including practice meditation, and doing this, and watch my breath,

195
00:14:00,758 --> 00:14:07,548
[nm]: And not meeting it, like on the existential level or presently doing things, and that that's when that boredom becomes anxiety and fear.

196
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:18,547
[nm]: But as I said, it's determined by your dependence on doing things, not by the actual solitude and neutral feeling.

